# Every variable here is OPTIONAL.
#
# With no .env file, Waypoint runs against the bundled fixtures in
# src/data/fixtures. The full UI works offline, including adding, editing and
# reviewing a place, which is kept in localStorage. Sign-in is hidden, since
# there is nothing to sign in to. That is the default `npm run dev` experience.
#
# Fill these four in to read and write live data in Firestore and to enable
# Google sign-in. Copy them from the Firebase console:
#   Project settings -> General -> Your apps -> SDK setup and configuration
#
# The web API key is a public client identifier rather than a secret: it ships
# in the JavaScript bundle either way, and what a caller may do is decided by
# firestore.rules. It lives here only so the repository is not tied to one
# Firebase project.
#
# There is no storage bucket in this list. Photographs are links to images
# already on the web, so nothing in the app talks to Cloud Storage.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Which shape to read. Leave unset for the schema this project seeds with
# scripts/seed-firestore.mjs: one document per place, reviews beneath it.
# Set to `legacy` to read the inherited 2021 database instead: places split
# across two collections, reviews joined by storage folder name, read-only.
# VITE_FIREBASE_SCHEMA=legacy

# Basemap tiles.
#
# With a MapTiler key the basemap is MapTiler Streets, in light and dark cuts of
# the same cartography. Get one from https://cloud.maptiler.com; the free tier
# covers a portfolio site.
#
# Like the Firebase key it is a public client identifier and ships in every tile
# URL the browser requests. Unlike it, it is metered, so restrict it to your own
# origins in the MapTiler console.
#
# VITE_MAPTILER_KEY=

# Without a key the map falls back to CARTO Voyager and Esri Dark Gray Canvas,
# which need no account, so `npm run dev` on a fresh clone still gets a map.
#
# Or name your own tile server, which wins over both of the above. The
# light/dark control switches between the two, so set both or the switch will
# only work one way, and pass whatever credit your provider asks for.
# VITE_TILE_URL=
# VITE_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=
# VITE_TILE_URL_DARK=
# VITE_TILE_ATTRIBUTION_DARK=
